-- title:
--   Stalk at a generic point of the special fibre: index one
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a discrete valuation ring (a commutative ring which is a domain and satisfies `IsDiscreteValuationRing`), let $Z$ be a scheme and let $z \colon Z \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a smooth morphism. Let $\zeta \in Z$ be a point whose image under the underlying map of $z$ is the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$, and assume that $\zeta$ is maximal under specialisation inside the special fibre: every $y \in Z$ with $y \rightsquigarrow \zeta$ (so that $\zeta$ lies in the closure of $\{y\}$) whose image is again the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ equals $\zeta$. Assume the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta}$ is given an $R$-algebra structure compatible with $z$, in the sense that $\operatorname{Spec} \mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta} \to Z$ (the canonical morphism `Z.fromSpecStalk ζ`) followed by $z$ equals the morphism of spectra induced by the structure map $R \to \mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta}$. Then $\mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta}$ is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring, the structure map $R \to \mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta}$ is a local homomorphism, and the pair satisfies `IsIndexOneExtension`, i.e. the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak{m}_R$ is exactly $\mathfrak{m}_{\mathcal{O}_{Z,\zeta}}$, and the extension of residue fields $\kappa(R) \to \kappa(\zeta)$ is formally smooth. The three instance data are produced as part of the existential conclusion.
--
--   This is the standard fact that the local ring of a smooth scheme over a discrete valuation ring at a generic point of an irreducible component of the special fibre is again a discrete valuation ring, unramified over the base (ramification index one). It is what makes extensions of ramification index one the correct test rings in the theory of weak Néron models, and it is used here to produce the index-one points and the component-reading data attached to a smooth $R$-scheme.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NeronModelInfra_isIndexOneExtension_stalk_of_smooth_of_forall_specializes.lean

